(*
 * SPDX-FileCopyrightText: nirapod-slhdsa contributors
 * SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
 *
 * SLHDSA_EUFCMA.eca
 * =================
 *
 * EUF-CMA of the FIPS 205 external interface (Algorithms 22 to 25, pure and
 * pre-hash requests under one key) for the parameter set P, from the
 * machine-checked EUF-CMA bound of SPHINCS+ in the imported security proof.
 *
 * Scheme. SLH_Internal is the internal scheme of FIPS 205 section 9:
 *
 *     keygen   SK.seed, SK.prf and PK.seed are n bytes drawn uniformly
 *              (the RBG of Algorithm 21), then slh_keygen_internal
 *     sign     slh_sign_internal with addrnd absent (deterministic)
 *     verify   slh_verify_internal
 *
 * and External(SLH_Internal) (ExternalFraming.ec) its external interface.
 *
 * Results.
 *
 *     internal_le_sp           a forger against SLH_Internal yields, through
 *                              the reduction R, a forger against the SPHINCS+
 *                              instance of SPHINCS_Instance with at least
 *                              the same success probability
 *     prf_proj                 for R, the PRF advantage against mkg equals
 *                              the PRF advantage against PRF_msg on
 *                              (opt_rand, M'), here (PK.seed, M'), under the
 *                              key SK.prf
 *     itsr_proj                for R, the ITSR advantage against mco is at
 *                              most the ITSR advantage against H_msg, with
 *                              the FIPS 205 index function, on
 *                              (PK.seed, PK.root, M')
 *     slhdsa_euf_cma           the external interface: the success
 *                              probability of any forger A is at most the
 *                              sum below, for the adversary R(B(A))
 *     spec_det_eq              the game against External(SLH_Internal) is
 *                              the game against Spec_Det, the external
 *                              interface as FIPS205_External.ec writes it
 *     slhdsa_euf_cma_spec      the bound of slhdsa_euf_cma for Spec_Det
 *
 * Spec_Det is the scheme of the specification itself: key generation is
 * the module SLH_DSA (Algorithm 21, its seeds drawn by dbytes), signing is
 * slh_sign and hash_slh_sign with addrnd absent, verification is
 * SLH_DSA.verify and SLH_DSA.hash_verify. It only dispatches on the kind of
 * request, returns SLH_DSA's (SK, PK) as the games' (pk, sk), and maps the
 * error indication None to the empty string. spec_det_eq rests on three
 * procedure equivalences: keygen_spec couples dnbytes with dbytes P.`n
 * through the subtype bijection, spec_det_sign and spec_det_verify reduce
 * to the operators case by case.
 *
 * The bound is concrete: a sum of success probabilities and advantages of
 * explicit adversaries built from A, with no numeric security level
 * derived. Its terms, each a standard property of a FIPS 205 function on
 * the inputs FIPS 205 gives it:
 *
 *  - PRF of PRF on the 32-byte ADRS and of PRF_msg on (opt_rand, M') with
 *    opt_rand an n-byte string, keyed by n-byte keys drawn uniformly;
 *  - interleaved target subset resilience of H_msg on (PK.seed, PK.root,
 *    M') with n-byte PK.seed and PK.root, keyed by the randomizer, with
 *    the index function that maps a digest to its FORS indices and
 *    instance;
 *  - the multi-target properties of F, H and T_l under the address types,
 *    as the imported proof states them: SM-DT-TCR of the FORS leaf hash F
 *    and SM-DT-DSPR against its second-preimage probability, both on n-byte
 *    inputs; SM-DT-TCR, -UD and -PRE of the WOTS+ chain hash F; SM-DT-TCR
 *    of H in the FORS and XMSS trees and of T_l compressing WOTS+ public
 *    keys and FORS roots;
 *  - collision resistance of the pre-hash functions, through the finder
 *    CF(SLH_Internal, A) of ExternalFraming.ec.
 *
 * PRF_msg and H_msg take their fixed-length fields as n-byte values, so
 * the concatenation they hash determines their arguments and the PRF and
 * ITSR terms are the standard properties. With byte strings of any length
 * in those fields, bytes could move between opt_rand and M', or between
 * PK.root and M', without changing the hash input, and both properties
 * would be false for every function.
 *
 * The TCR, UD and PRE terms take bit strings of any length. The tweakable
 * hash of SPHINCS_Instance.eca hashes strings of whole bytes as FIPS 205
 * does and domain-separates every other string (see its header), so
 * distinct inputs never reach the same input of SHAKE256 or SHA-2, and
 * none of these games is won by a structural collision of the model. The
 * DSPR term is stated on n-byte inputs, where its second-preimage
 * predicate ranges over n-byte strings only.
 *
 * The imported proof states its message-key terms for the SPHINCS+
 * instance message (PK || opt_rand, M'). There mkg ignores PK.seed and
 * PK.root and mco ignores opt_rand, so neither is a PRF or ITSR on that
 * type. prf_proj and itsr_proj restate them for PRF_msg and H_msg through
 * the adversaries PP and PI. R signs every message with the same prefix
 * PK || PK.seed (deterministic signing is Algorithm 19 with opt_rand =
 * PK.seed), so the mkg queries are the PRF_msg queries (PK.seed, M') one to
 * one, and R's forgery, new on the instance type, stays new on the inputs
 * of H_msg.
 *
 * Hypotheses: A terminates whenever its signing oracle does, and A does not
 * read or write the state of the games and reductions involved (the module
 * restrictions of the statement). Nothing is assumed about the hash
 * functions: each property appears as a term of the bound.
 *
 * Scope.
 *
 *  - Deterministic signing for every query: a key used for both
 *    deterministic and hedged signatures is not covered.
 *    SLHDSA_Hedged.eca covers hedged signing (addrnd present).
 *  - The result is about the EasyCrypt operators of FIPS 205 in spec/, not
 *    about the Jasmin code; relating the two is a separate correctness
 *    proof, which is open.
 *  - The signature games type a signature as a byte string, so the error
 *    indication None of slh_sign and hash_slh_sign is read as the empty
 *    string.
 *  - The randomness of key generation is modelled as uniform n-byte
 *    strings, the dbytes of SLH_DSA.keygen.
 *  - Software-visible behaviour only: faults and physical leakage are out
 *    of scope of this theorem.
 *)

require import AllCore List Distr DList FMap.
from Jasmin require import JWord.
require import Bytes FIPS205_Params FIPS205_Hash FIPS205_Internal FIPS205_External FIPS205_XMSS FIPS205_Address_Props.
require import ExternalFraming.
require SPHINCS_Refinement.
require (*--*) KeyedHashFunctions.

clone include SPHINCS_Refinement.

(* ------------------------------------------------------------------ *)
(* The internal scheme of FIPS 205 section 9                          *)

module SLH_Internal : DSI.Stateless.Scheme = {
  proc keygen() : bytes * bytes = {
    var ss, sprf, ps, k;
    ss <$ dnbytes;
    sprf <$ dnbytes;
    ps <$ dnbytes;
    k <- slh_keygen_internal P (NBytes.val ss) (NBytes.val sprf) (NBytes.val ps);
    return (k.`2, k.`1);
  }

  proc sign(sk : bytes, m : bytes) : bytes = {
    return slh_sign_internal P m sk None;
  }

  proc verify(pk : bytes, m : bytes, s : bytes) : bool = {
    return slh_verify_internal P m s pk;
  }
}.

lemma SLH_verify_ll : islossless SLH_Internal.verify.
proof. by proc. qed.

(* ------------------------------------------------------------------ *)
(* Termination of SPHINCS+ verification                               *)

lemma pkWOTS_from_sigWOTS_ll : islossless SP.FSSLXMTWES.WTWES.WOTS_TW_ES.pkWOTS_from_sigWOTS.
proof.
proc; while true (SP.len - size pkWOTS); first by move=> z; auto; smt(size_rcons).
by auto; smt().
qed.

lemma root_from_sig_ll : islossless SP.FSSLXMTWES.FL_SL_XMSS_MT_ES.root_from_sigFLSLXMSSMTTW.
proof.
proc; while true (P.`d - i).
+ by move=> z; wp; call pkWOTS_from_sigWOTS_ll; auto; smt().
by auto; smt().
qed.

lemma pkFORS_from_sig_ll : islossless SP.FTWES.FL_FORS_ES.pkFORS_from_sigFORSTW.
proof.
proc; wp; while true (P.`k - size roots); first by move=> z; auto; smt(size_rcons).
by auto; smt().
qed.

lemma SP_verify_ll : islossless SP.SPHINCS_PLUS.verify.
proof. by proc; call root_from_sig_ll; call pkFORS_from_sig_ll; auto. qed.

(* ------------------------------------------------------------------ *)
(* From the internal scheme to SPHINCS+                               *)

(* The reduction: run A on the byte encoding of the SPHINCS+ public key,
   sign A's messages M as the pairs (PK || PK.seed, M) (opt_rand = PK.seed),
   encode the signatures, and decode A's forgery. *)
module R (A : DSI.Stateless.Adv_EUFCMA) (O : SP.DSS.Stateless.SOracle_CMA) = {
  var pkb : bytes
  var pkm : bytes

  module O' = {
    proc sign(m : bytes) : bytes = {
      var s;
      s <@ O.sign((pkm, m));
      return enc_sig s;
    }
  }

  proc forge(pk : SP.pkSPHINCSPLUSTW) : (bytes * bytes) * SP.sigSPHINCSPLUSTW = {
    var m, s;
    pkb <- NBytes.val pk.`2 ++ enc pk.`1;
    pkm <- pkb ++ NBytes.val pk.`2;
    (m, s) <@ A(O').forge(pkb);
    return ((pkm, m), dec_sig s);
  }
}.

(* Deterministic signing is hedged signing with opt_rand = PK.seed. *)
lemma sign_det (M x y z w : bytes) :
  size x = P.`n => size y = P.`n => size z = P.`n => size w = P.`n =>
  slh_sign_internal P M (x ++ y ++ z ++ w) None
  = slh_sign_internal P M (x ++ y ++ z ++ w) (Some z).
proof.
move=> hx hy hz hw; have [_ [_ [h3 _]]] := key_fields x y z w hx hy hz hw.
by rewrite /slh_sign_internal /= h3.
qed.

(* The secret key of SLH_Internal held by the oracle, the SPHINCS+ secret
   key and the public key bytes held by the reduction, with the common
   root. *)
pred keys_rel (skI : bytes) (skS : nbytes * nbytes * nbytes) (pkb : bytes) =
  exists (r : SP.dgstblock),
    pkb = NBytes.val skS.`3 ++ enc r
    /\ skI = NBytes.val skS.`2 ++ NBytes.val skS.`1 ++ NBytes.val skS.`3 ++ enc r.

section Reduction.

declare module A <: DSI.Stateless.Adv_EUFCMA
  {-R, -DSI.Stateless.O_CMA_Default, -SP.DSS.Stateless.O_CMA_Default}.

lemma verify_pre (rootA : SP.dgstblock) psA (rA M b : bytes) :
  phoare [SP.SPHINCS_PLUS.verify :
            arg = ((rootA, psA), (NBytes.val psA ++ enc rootA ++ rA, M), dec_sig b) /\ size b = sig_length P
            ==> res = slh_verify_internal P M b (NBytes.val psA ++ enc rootA)] = 1%r.
proof.
case: (size b = sig_length P) => hb.
+ by conseq (verify_refine rootA psA rA M b hb) => /#.
by exfalso; move=> &hr.
qed.

lemma oracle_eq :
  equiv [DSI.Stateless.O_CMA_Default(SLH_Internal).sign
         ~ R(A, SP.DSS.Stateless.O_CMA_Default(SP.SPHINCS_PLUS)).O'.sign :
         ={m} /\ keys_rel DSI.Stateless.O_CMA_Default.sk{1} SP.DSS.Stateless.O_CMA_Default.sk{2} R.pkb{2}
         /\ R.pkm{2} = R.pkb{2} ++ NBytes.val SP.DSS.Stateless.O_CMA_Default.sk{2}.`3
         /\ SP.DSS.Stateless.O_CMA_Default.qs{2} = map (fun x => (R.pkm{2}, x)) DSI.Stateless.O_CMA_Default.qs{1}
         ==> ={res} /\ keys_rel DSI.Stateless.O_CMA_Default.sk{1} SP.DSS.Stateless.O_CMA_Default.sk{2} R.pkb{2}
         /\ R.pkm{2} = R.pkb{2} ++ NBytes.val SP.DSS.Stateless.O_CMA_Default.sk{2}.`3
         /\ SP.DSS.Stateless.O_CMA_Default.qs{2} = map (fun x => (R.pkm{2}, x)) DSI.Stateless.O_CMA_Default.qs{1}].
proof.
proc; inline SP.DSS.Stateless.O_CMA_Default(SP.SPHINCS_PLUS).sign SLH_Internal.sign.
conseq (_: m{1} = m{2}
           /\ (exists r, R.pkb{2} = NBytes.val SP.DSS.Stateless.O_CMA_Default.sk{2}.`3 ++ enc r
                /\ DSI.Stateless.O_CMA_Default.sk{1}
                    = NBytes.val SP.DSS.Stateless.O_CMA_Default.sk{2}.`2
                      ++ NBytes.val SP.DSS.Stateless.O_CMA_Default.sk{2}.`1
                      ++ NBytes.val SP.DSS.Stateless.O_CMA_Default.sk{2}.`3 ++ enc r)
           /\ R.pkm{2} = R.pkb{2} ++ NBytes.val SP.DSS.Stateless.O_CMA_Default.sk{2}.`3
           /\ SP.DSS.Stateless.O_CMA_Default.qs{2}
               = map (fun x => (R.pkm{2}, x)) DSI.Stateless.O_CMA_Default.qs{1}
           ==> _) => //.
elim* => r.
exlim (SP.DSS.Stateless.O_CMA_Default.sk{2}).`1, (SP.DSS.Stateless.O_CMA_Default.sk{2}).`2,
      (SP.DSS.Stateless.O_CMA_Default.sk{2}).`3, m{2} => ms ss ps M.
wp; call{2} (sign_refine ms ss ps r (NBytes.val ps) M (nval_size ps)).
auto => /> &1 &2; split; first by case: (SP.DSS.Stateless.O_CMA_Default.sk{2}).
move=> _ sg -> /=; split.
+ by rewrite sign_det // ?nval_size ?size_enc.
split; first by exists r.
by rewrite map_rcons.
qed.

lemma internal_le_sp &m :
  Pr[DSI.Stateless.EUF_CMA(SLH_Internal, A, DSI.Stateless.O_CMA_Default).main() @ &m : res]
  <= Pr[SP.DSS.Stateless.EUF_CMA(SP.SPHINCS_PLUS, R(A), SP.DSS.Stateless.O_CMA_Default).main() @ &m : res].
proof.
byequiv => //; proc.
inline SLH_Internal.keygen SP.SPHINCS_PLUS.keygen.
inline DSI.Stateless.O_CMA_Default(SLH_Internal).init SP.DSS.Stateless.O_CMA_Default(SP.SPHINCS_PLUS).init.
inline R(A, SP.DSS.Stateless.O_CMA_Default(SP.SPHINCS_PLUS)).forge.
inline DSI.Stateless.O_CMA_Default(SLH_Internal).fresh SP.DSS.Stateless.O_CMA_Default(SP.SPHINCS_PLUS).fresh.
inline SLH_Internal.verify.
swap{1} 1 1.
seq 3 4 : (={glob A} /\ sprf{1} = ms{2} /\ ss{1} = ss{2} /\ ps{1} = ps{2} /\ ad{2} = SP.adz).
+ by wp; rnd; rnd; rnd; wp; skip.
exlim ss{2}, ps{2} => s0 p0.
seq 0 1 : (={glob A} /\ sprf{1} = ms{2} /\ ss{1} = s0 /\ ss{2} = s0 /\ ps{1} = p0 /\ ps{2} = p0
           /\ enc root{2} = xmss_node P (NBytes.val s0) 0 P.`hp (NBytes.val p0) (mk_adrs (P.`d - 1) 0 0 0 0 0)).
+ by call{2} (gen_root_ph s0 p0); skip => /> /#.
seq 6 10 : (keys_rel DSI.Stateless.O_CMA_Default.sk{1} SP.DSS.Stateless.O_CMA_Default.sk{2} R.pkb{2}
           /\ SP.DSS.Stateless.O_CMA_Default.qs{2}
               = map (fun x => (R.pkm{2}, x)) DSI.Stateless.O_CMA_Default.qs{1}
           /\ m{1} = m0{2} /\ sig{1} = s{2} /\ pk{1} = R.pkb{2}
           /\ pk{2} = (root{2}, ps{2}) /\ R.pkb{2} = NBytes.val ps{2} ++ enc root{2}
           /\ R.pkm{2} = R.pkb{2} ++ NBytes.val ps{2}).
+ call (_: keys_rel DSI.Stateless.O_CMA_Default.sk{1} SP.DSS.Stateless.O_CMA_Default.sk{2} R.pkb{2}
           /\ R.pkm{2} = R.pkb{2} ++ NBytes.val SP.DSS.Stateless.O_CMA_Default.sk{2}.`3
           /\ SP.DSS.Stateless.O_CMA_Default.qs{2}
               = map (fun x => (R.pkm{2}, x)) DSI.Stateless.O_CMA_Default.qs{1}).
  + by conseq oracle_eq.
  wp; skip => /> &2 hr.
  rewrite (keygen_bytes s0 ms{2} p0 root{2} hr) /=.
  by exists root{2}.
exlim sig{1}, root{2}, ps{2}, m{1} => b r p M.
case (size b = sig_length P).
+ wp; call{2} (verify_pre r p (NBytes.val p) M b).
  wp; skip => &1 &2 H; move: H => [#] hb hr hp hM _ hqs hm hsig hpk1 hpk2 hpkb hpkm hsz /=.
  split; first smt().
  move=> _ v hv [hval hfresh]; split.
  + by move: hval; rewrite hv hpk1 hpkb hb hr hp hM.
  move: hfresh; rewrite hqs -hm; apply contra => /mapP [x [hx /= ->]] //.
wp; call{2} SP_verify_ll.
by auto => />.
qed.

end section Reduction.

(* ------------------------------------------------------------------ *)
(* PRF_msg and H_msg on their own inputs                              *)

(* The imported bound states its message-key PRF term for mkg and its
   ITSR term for mco, both keyed functions of the instance message
   (PK || opt_rand, M'). Neither is a meaningful assumption on that type:
   mkg ignores PK.seed and PK.root, and mco ignores opt_rand. The clones
   below give PRF_msg and H_msg their own input types, and the
   adversaries PP and PI carry a distinguisher or ITSR adversary from the
   instance type over to them. *)

(* PRF_msg(SK.prf, opt_rand, M') as a keyed function of (opt_rand, M').
   opt_rand has the type of n-byte strings: PRF_msg hashes opt_rand || M',
   which is injective in the pair only when the length of opt_rand is
   fixed. *)
op prf_msg (k : nbytes) (x : nbytes * bytes) : nbytes =
  NBytes.insubd (PRF_msg P (NBytes.val k) (NBytes.val x.`1) x.`2).

clone KeyedHashFunctions as PRFMsg with
  type key_t <- nbytes,
  type in_t <- nbytes * bytes,
  type out_t <- nbytes,
  op f <- prf_msg
proof *.

clone PRFMsg.PRF as PRFMsg_PRF with
  op dkey <- dnbytes,
  op doutm x <- dnbytes
proof *.
realize dkey_ll by exact dnbytes_ll.
realize doutm_ll by move=> _; exact dnbytes_ll.

(* A distinguisher against mkg made into one against PRF_msg: each query
   (PK || opt_rand, M') is asked as (opt_rand, M'). *)
module PP (C : SP.MKG_PRF.Adv_PRF) (O : PRFMsg_PRF.Oracle_PRF) = {
  module O' : SP.MKG_PRF.Oracle_PRF = {
    proc init(b : bool) : unit = { }

    proc query(x : bytes * bytes) : nbytes = {
      var y;
      y <@ O.query((NBytes.insubd (slice x.`1 (2 * P.`n) (3 * P.`n)), x.`2));
      return y;
    }
  }

  proc distinguish() : bool = {
    var b;
    b <@ C(O').distinguish();
    return b;
  }
}.

(* H_msg(R, PK.seed, PK.root, M') followed by the digest split of
   Algorithm 19, lines 6 to 10, in the model's representation: the FORS
   message bits and the index of the FORS instance. PK.seed and PK.root
   are n-byte strings, so that R || PK.seed || PK.root || M' determines
   the triple. *)
op hmsg (k : nbytes) (x : nbytes * nbytes * bytes) : SP.FTWES.msgFORSTW * SP.index =
  let digest = H_msg P (NBytes.val k) (NBytes.val x.`1) (NBytes.val x.`2) x.`3 in
  let (md, it, il) = split_digest P digest in
  (SP.FTWES.BLKAL.insubd (take (P.`k * P.`a) (msb_bits md)), SP.Index.insubd (it * 2 ^ P.`hp + il)).

(* The inputs of H_msg in a message of the instance. *)
op pmsg (m : bytes * bytes) : nbytes * nbytes * bytes =
  (NBytes.insubd (slice m.`1 0 P.`n), NBytes.insubd (slice m.`1 P.`n (2 * P.`n)), m.`2).

(* On instance messages that carry a public key, mco is H_msg on pmsg. *)
lemma mco_hmsg k (m : bytes * bytes) :
  2 * P.`n <= size m.`1 => SP.FTWES.mco k m = hmsg k (pmsg m).
proof.
move=> hm; have hn := n_bounds.
rewrite /hmsg /pmsg /= !NBytes.insubdK ?size_slice //; smt().
qed.

clone KeyedHashFunctions as HMsg with
  type key_t <- nbytes,
  type in_t <- nbytes * nbytes * bytes,
  type out_t <- SP.FTWES.msgFORSTW * SP.index,
  op f <- hmsg
proof *.

clone HMsg.ITSR as HMsg_ITSR with
  op g <- SP.FTWES.g,
  op dkey <- dnbytes
proof *.
realize dkey_ll by exact dnbytes_ll.

(* An ITSR adversary against mco made into one against H_msg: each query
   and the final pair are mapped to the inputs of H_msg. *)
module PI (C : SP.FTWES.MCO_ITSR.Adv_ITSR) (O : HMsg_ITSR.Oracle_ITSR) = {
  module O' : SP.FTWES.MCO_ITSR.Oracle_ITSR = {
    proc init() : unit = { }

    proc query(x : bytes * bytes) : nbytes = {
      var k;
      k <@ O.query(pmsg x);
      return k;
    }

    proc get_targets() : (nbytes * (bytes * bytes)) list = {
      return [];
    }
  }

  proc find() : nbytes * (nbytes * nbytes * bytes) = {
    var k, x;
    (k, x) <@ C(O').find();
    return (k, pmsg x);
  }
}.

op pi (kx : nbytes * (bytes * bytes)) : nbytes * (nbytes * nbytes * bytes) = (kx.`1, pmsg kx.`2).

(* The index tuples of mco on an instance message are those of H_msg on
   its inputs, so coverage by a target list carries over to its image. *)
lemma itsr_cover (ts : (nbytes * (bytes * bytes)) list) (k : nbytes) (x : bytes * bytes) :
  2 * P.`n <= size x.`1 =>
  (forall kx, kx \in ts => 2 * P.`n <= size kx.`2.`1) =>
  (forall t, t \in SP.FTWES.MCO_ITSR.h k x =>
     t \in flatten (map (fun (kx : nbytes * (bytes * bytes)) => SP.FTWES.MCO_ITSR.h kx.`1 kx.`2) ts))
  => forall t, t \in HMsg_ITSR.h k (pmsg x) =>
     t \in flatten (map (fun (kx : nbytes * (nbytes * nbytes * bytes)) => HMsg_ITSR.h kx.`1 kx.`2) (map pi ts)).
proof.
have hh : forall k' (x' : bytes * bytes), 2 * P.`n <= size x'.`1 =>
  SP.FTWES.MCO_ITSR.h k' x' = HMsg_ITSR.h k' (pmsg x').
+ move=> k' x' hx'; have hn := n_bounds.
  by rewrite /SP.FTWES.MCO_ITSR.h /HMsg_ITSR.h /hmsg /pmsg /= !NBytes.insubdK ?size_slice //; smt().
move=> hx hts hcov t; rewrite -(hh _ _ hx) => /hcov; rewrite -map_comp.
have -> : map ((fun (kx : nbytes * (nbytes * nbytes * bytes)) => HMsg_ITSR.h kx.`1 kx.`2) \o pi) ts
          = map (fun (kx : nbytes * (bytes * bytes)) => SP.FTWES.MCO_ITSR.h kx.`1 kx.`2) ts.
+ by apply eq_in_map => kx /hts hkx; rewrite /(\o) /pi /= (hh _ _ hkx).
by [].
qed.

(* ------------------------------------------------------------------ *)
(* The two terms for the reduction R                                   *)

(* R puts the same prefix pkm = PK || PK.seed on every query, so the
   mkg queries are the PRF_msg queries (PK.seed, M') one to one. *)
op pseed (pkm : bytes) : nbytes = NBytes.insubd (slice pkm (2 * P.`n) (3 * P.`n)).

pred prf_rel (pkm : bytes) (mS : (bytes * bytes, nbytes) fmap) (mF : (nbytes * bytes, nbytes) fmap) =
  size pkm = 3 * P.`n
  /\ forall r M, mF.[(r, M)] = if r = pseed pkm then mS.[(pkm, M)] else None.

lemma prf_rel_get pkm mS mF (M : bytes) :
  prf_rel pkm mS mF => mF.[(pseed pkm, M)] = mS.[(pkm, M)].
proof. by move=> [_ h]; rewrite h. qed.

lemma prf_rel_set pkm mS mF (M : bytes) (y : nbytes) :
  prf_rel pkm mS mF =>
  prf_rel pkm mS.[(pkm, M) <- y] mF.[(pseed pkm, M) <- y].
proof.
move=> [hs h]; split => // r M'; rewrite !get_setE h.
by case: (r = pseed pkm) => [-> /= | /#].
qed.

(* The real branches agree: mkg reads exactly the n bytes that PP passes. *)
lemma prf_msg_pseed k pkm mS mF (M : bytes) :
  prf_rel pkm mS mF => prf_msg k (pseed pkm, M) = SP.mkg k (pkm, M).
proof.
move=> [hs _]; have hn := n_bounds.
by rewrite /prf_msg /pseed /= NBytes.insubdK // size_slice /#.
qed.

section PRFProjection.

declare module A <: DSI.Stateless.Adv_EUFCMA
  {-R, -SP.R_MKGPRF_EUFCMA, -SP.MKG_PRF.O_PRF_Default, -PRFMsg_PRF.O_PRF_Default}.

local lemma prf_oracle :
  equiv [R(A, SP.R_MKGPRF_EUFCMA(R(A), SP.MKG_PRF.O_PRF_Default).O_CMA).O'.sign
         ~ R(A, SP.R_MKGPRF_EUFCMA(R(A), PP(SP.R_MKGPRF_EUFCMA(R(A)), PRFMsg_PRF.O_PRF_Default).O').O_CMA).O'.sign :
         ={m, R.pkb, R.pkm, glob SP.R_MKGPRF_EUFCMA}
         /\ ={b, k}(SP.MKG_PRF.O_PRF_Default, PRFMsg_PRF.O_PRF_Default)
         /\ prf_rel R.pkm{1} SP.MKG_PRF.O_PRF_Default.m{1} PRFMsg_PRF.O_PRF_Default.m{2}
         ==> ={res, R.pkb, R.pkm, glob SP.R_MKGPRF_EUFCMA}
         /\ ={b, k}(SP.MKG_PRF.O_PRF_Default, PRFMsg_PRF.O_PRF_Default)
         /\ prf_rel R.pkm{1} SP.MKG_PRF.O_PRF_Default.m{1} PRFMsg_PRF.O_PRF_Default.m{2}].
proof.
proc.
inline SP.R_MKGPRF_EUFCMA(R(A), SP.MKG_PRF.O_PRF_Default).O_CMA.sign
       SP.R_MKGPRF_EUFCMA(R(A), PP(SP.R_MKGPRF_EUFCMA(R(A)), PRFMsg_PRF.O_PRF_Default).O').O_CMA.sign.
inline SP.MKG_PRF.O_PRF_Default.query PP(SP.R_MKGPRF_EUFCMA(R(A)), PRFMsg_PRF.O_PRF_Default).O'.query
       PRFMsg_PRF.O_PRF_Default.query.
seq 2 2 : (={m0, ad, m, R.pkb, R.pkm, glob SP.R_MKGPRF_EUFCMA}
           /\ ={b, k}(SP.MKG_PRF.O_PRF_Default, PRFMsg_PRF.O_PRF_Default)
           /\ prf_rel R.pkm{1} SP.MKG_PRF.O_PRF_Default.m{1} PRFMsg_PRF.O_PRF_Default.m{2}
           /\ m0{1} = (R.pkm{1}, m{1})).
+ by auto.
seq 3 5 : (={m0, ad, m, mk, R.pkb, R.pkm, glob SP.R_MKGPRF_EUFCMA}
           /\ ={b, k}(SP.MKG_PRF.O_PRF_Default, PRFMsg_PRF.O_PRF_Default)
           /\ prf_rel R.pkm{1} SP.MKG_PRF.O_PRF_Default.m{1} PRFMsg_PRF.O_PRF_Default.m{2}).
+ sp.
  conseq (_: ={m0, ad, m, R.pkb, R.pkm, glob SP.R_MKGPRF_EUFCMA}
             /\ ={b, k}(SP.MKG_PRF.O_PRF_Default, PRFMsg_PRF.O_PRF_Default)
             /\ prf_rel R.pkm{1} SP.MKG_PRF.O_PRF_Default.m{1} PRFMsg_PRF.O_PRF_Default.m{2}
             /\ x{1} = (R.pkm{1}, m{1})
             /\ x0{2} = (pseed R.pkm{1}, m{1}) ==> _).
  + by move=> &1 &2 [#] -> -> -> 9!-> hb hk hrel hm0; rewrite hm0.
  if => //.
  + if.
    + by move=> /> &1 &2 *; rewrite !domE; smt(prf_rel_get).
    + auto => &1 &2 [#] 12!-> hrel -> -> _ _ y hy /=; rewrite !get_set_sameE /= hy /=.
      exact (prf_rel_set _ _ _ _ _ hrel).
    by auto => /> &1 &2 *; smt(prf_rel_get).
  by auto => &1 &2 [#] 12!-> hrel -> -> _ /=; rewrite (prf_msg_pseed _ _ _ _ _ hrel).
sim / (={b, k}(SP.MKG_PRF.O_PRF_Default, PRFMsg_PRF.O_PRF_Default)
       /\ prf_rel R.pkm{1} SP.MKG_PRF.O_PRF_Default.m{1} PRFMsg_PRF.O_PRF_Default.m{2})
    : (={s, R.pkb, R.pkm, glob SP.R_MKGPRF_EUFCMA}).
qed.

local lemma prf_dist :
  equiv [SP.R_MKGPRF_EUFCMA(R(A), SP.MKG_PRF.O_PRF_Default).distinguish
         ~ SP.R_MKGPRF_EUFCMA(R(A), PP(SP.R_MKGPRF_EUFCMA(R(A)), PRFMsg_PRF.O_PRF_Default).O').distinguish :
         ={glob A}
         /\ ={b, k}(SP.MKG_PRF.O_PRF_Default, PRFMsg_PRF.O_PRF_Default)
         /\ SP.MKG_PRF.O_PRF_Default.m{1} = empty /\ PRFMsg_PRF.O_PRF_Default.m{2} = empty
         ==> ={res}].
proof.
proc.
inline R(A, SP.R_MKGPRF_EUFCMA(R(A), SP.MKG_PRF.O_PRF_Default).O_CMA).forge
       R(A, SP.R_MKGPRF_EUFCMA(R(A), PP(SP.R_MKGPRF_EUFCMA(R(A)), PRFMsg_PRF.O_PRF_Default).O').O_CMA).forge.
seq 12 12 : (={glob A, glob SP.R_MKGPRF_EUFCMA, pk}
             /\ ={b, k}(SP.MKG_PRF.O_PRF_Default, PRFMsg_PRF.O_PRF_Default)
             /\ SP.MKG_PRF.O_PRF_Default.m{1} = empty /\ PRFMsg_PRF.O_PRF_Default.m{2} = empty).
+ sim / (={b, k}(SP.MKG_PRF.O_PRF_Default, PRFMsg_PRF.O_PRF_Default)
         /\ SP.MKG_PRF.O_PRF_Default.m{1} = empty /\ PRFMsg_PRF.O_PRF_Default.m{2} = empty)
      : (={glob A, glob SP.R_MKGPRF_EUFCMA, pk}).
seq 3 3 : (={glob A, glob SP.R_MKGPRF_EUFCMA, pk, pk0, R.pkb, R.pkm}
           /\ ={b, k}(SP.MKG_PRF.O_PRF_Default, PRFMsg_PRF.O_PRF_Default)
           /\ prf_rel R.pkm{1} SP.MKG_PRF.O_PRF_Default.m{1} PRFMsg_PRF.O_PRF_Default.m{2}).
+ auto => /> *; split => [|r M]; [rewrite size_cat size_cat nval_size size_enc; ring | by rewrite !emptyE if_same].
seq 1 1 : (={glob A, glob SP.R_MKGPRF_EUFCMA, pk, pk0, R.pkb, R.pkm, m, s}).
+ call (: ={R.pkb, R.pkm, glob SP.R_MKGPRF_EUFCMA}
          /\ ={b, k}(SP.MKG_PRF.O_PRF_Default, PRFMsg_PRF.O_PRF_Default)
          /\ prf_rel R.pkm{1} SP.MKG_PRF.O_PRF_Default.m{1} PRFMsg_PRF.O_PRF_Default.m{2}).
  + by conseq prf_oracle.
  by auto.
sim.
qed.

lemma prf_proj b &m :
  Pr[SP.MKG_PRF.PRF(SP.R_MKGPRF_EUFCMA(R(A)), SP.MKG_PRF.O_PRF_Default).main(b) @ &m : res]
  = Pr[PRFMsg_PRF.PRF(PP(SP.R_MKGPRF_EUFCMA(R(A))), PRFMsg_PRF.O_PRF_Default).main(b) @ &m : res].
proof.
byequiv => //; proc.
inline SP.MKG_PRF.O_PRF_Default.init PRFMsg_PRF.O_PRF_Default.init
       PP(SP.R_MKGPRF_EUFCMA(R(A)), PRFMsg_PRF.O_PRF_Default).distinguish.
wp; call prf_dist; auto.
qed.

end section PRFProjection.

(* R's forgery (pkm, M') is new on the instance type; every target carries
   the same pkm, so it stays new on the inputs of H_msg. *)
lemma itsr_final (pkm : bytes) (ts : (nbytes * (bytes * bytes)) list) (k : nbytes) (M : bytes) :
  2 * P.`n <= size pkm =>
  (forall k' x', (k', x') \in ts => x'.`1 = pkm) =>
     (forall t, t \in SP.FTWES.MCO_ITSR.h k (pkm, M) =>
         t \in flatten (map (fun (kx : nbytes * (bytes * bytes)) => SP.FTWES.MCO_ITSR.h kx.`1 kx.`2) ts))
  /\ ! (k, (pkm, M)) \in ts
  => (forall t, t \in HMsg_ITSR.h k (pmsg (pkm, M)) =>
         t \in flatten (map (fun (kx : nbytes * (nbytes * nbytes * bytes)) => HMsg_ITSR.h kx.`1 kx.`2) (map pi ts)))
  /\ ! (k, pmsg (pkm, M)) \in map pi ts.
proof.
move=> hsz hts [hcov hnew]; split.
+ have hts' : forall (kx : nbytes * (bytes * bytes)), kx \in ts => 2 * P.`n <= size kx.`2.`1.
  + by move=> -[k' x'] hin /=; rewrite (hts _ _ hin).
  exact (itsr_cover ts k (pkm, M) hsz hts' hcov).
move: hnew; apply contra => /mapP [[k' x'] [hin /= [hk hx]]].
have h1 := hts _ _ hin.
have h2 : x'.`2 = M by move: hx; rewrite /pmsg /=; smt().
by rewrite hk (_ : (pkm, M) = x') 1:/#.
qed.

section ITSRProjection.

